        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "084e5504-7f1e-594b-bad1-9c85ed1c1c73",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Alex da Kid, Eminem, Rihanna, Dr. Dre, Nicki Minaj, B.o.B, Hayley Williams, Diddy, Skylar Grey, Imagine Dragons, Cheryl, Candice Pillay, Sam Harris, Kanye West\n- Songs: I Need a Doctor, Massive Attack, Airplanes, Love the Way You Lie, Coming Home, Radioactive, Under The Sun, American Oxygen\n- Albums: Recovery\n\nFacts:\n- Alex da Kid gained recognition for producing hit singles for multiple artists across genres, including Dr. Dre's \"I Need a Doctor,\" Nicki Minaj's \"Massive Attack,\" B.o.B's \"Airplanes\" featuring Hayley Williams, Eminem's \"Love the Way You Lie\" featuring Rihanna, Diddy's \"Coming Home\" with Dirty Money featuring Skylar Grey, Imagine Dragons' \"Radioactive,\" and Cheryl's \"Under The Sun.\"\n- \"Love the Way You Lie\" is a song by Eminem featuring Rihanna from Eminem's seventh studio album \"Recovery\" (2010).\n- \"American Oxygen\" was written by Alex da Kid, Candice Pillay, Sam Harris, and Rihanna, and it was produced by Alex da Kid and Kanye West.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "fc0f801e-de3a-529d-b06d-869a4df6b933",
        "text": "Page: Alex da Kid. Sentence: He has gained recognition for producing several hit singles for a plethora of artists in various music genres, such as Dr. Dre (\"I Need a Doctor\"), Nicki Minaj (\"Massive Attack\"), B.o.B (\"Airplanes\" featuring Hayley Williams), Eminem (\"Love the Way You Lie\" featuring Rihanna), Diddy (\"Coming Home\" with Dirty Money featuring Skylar Grey), Imagine Dragons (\"Radioactive\") and Cheryl (\"Under The Sun\").\nPage: Love the Way You Lie. Sentence: \"Love the Way You Lie\" is a song recorded by the American rapper Eminem, featuring the Barbadian singer Rihanna, from Eminem's seventh studio album \"Recovery\" (2010).\nPage: American Oxygen. Sentence: It was written by Alex da Kid, Candice Pillay, Sam Harris and Rihanna; Alex da Kid and Kanye West produced it.",
